## Correct misleading comment on ExternalLogin's IsNotAllowed fallback

### Status
Done.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
The comment on `ExternalLogin.cshtml.cs`'s `OnGetCallbackAsync` `IsNotAllowed` branch describes
it as a rare fallback that "shouldn't be reachable" — but it's actually the expected outcome the
very next time someone whose confirmation-form email didn't match the provider's claim signs in
again via Google.

### Motivation
A future contributor reading "shouldn't be reachable... kept as a safe fallback" could
reasonably conclude this branch is dead code and remove it, silently breaking sign-in for every
account created via that path until its email gets confirmed.

### Proposed Changes
Reword the comment at `ExternalLogin.cshtml.cs`'s `IsNotAllowed` branch to state plainly that
this is the normal, expected path for any account created via the email-mismatch branch of
`OnPostConfirmationAsync`, reached on every sign-in attempt until that account's email is
confirmed.

### Acceptance Criteria
- The comment no longer characterizes this branch as unreachable or a rare fallback.

### Out of Scope
- No behavior change — comment wording only.

